WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.209 --> 00:00:01.290
(gentle music)

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:03.340
- [Narrator] In late June
footage from crypto mining farms

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:05.770
in China started popping up on Douyin,

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:08.140
the Chinese version of Tiktok.

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:10.410
Machines that mine
cryptocurrencies like Bitcoin

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.810
were being dismantled and packed up.

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:14.070
These facilities in China

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:17.420
have produced up to 3/4 of
the world's supply of Bitcoin.

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:19.850
But that started to change
when about a month earlier,

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:21.570
one of China's most senior officials

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:22.550
at the central government

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:24.960
pledged to crack down on Bitcoin mining.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.960
But he didn't specify what
measures he would take

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.480
against crypto miners.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:31.284
However, some local authorities
began taking action.

00:00:31.284 --> 00:00:33.833
- (woman speaking foreign language)

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:35.170
- [Narrator] A government
backed news outlets

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:37.980
showed social media footage
of miners turning off machines

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:39.930
after authorities in Sichuan province,

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:42.580
ordered electricity providers
to stop supplying power

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:43.560
to these facilities.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:45.830
- All of this equipment came offline.

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:47.740
There have been huge ripple effects.

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:48.760
- [Narrator] After Beijing's warning,

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:50.300
the global mining hash rate,

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.980
that's the measurement
of the computing power

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:55.440
used to mine Bitcoins
dropped by almost 50%.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:58.270
- The sudden drop just means
everyone who continues mining

00:00:58.270 --> 00:01:00.580
now has a bigger piece of the pie.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:02.710
- [Narrator] So miners around
the world are taking advantage

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:04.076
of the Exodus of Chinese miners

00:01:04.076 --> 00:01:05.920
to expand their own businesses

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:08.400
and hoping that the power
behind cryptocurrencies

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:11.810
is becoming less dependent
on a single country.

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:14.920
First, you need to understand
how crypto miners make money.

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:17.190
- Bitcoin miners are
effectively participating

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:20.780
in a global lottery, every
time they start mining Bitcoin.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:21.680
- [Narrator] Brandon Arvanaghi

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:23.150
used to be a security engineer

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:25.160
at a crypto exchange,
and now runs a company

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:27.030
that helps miners set up facilities.

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:29.450
- Miners are solving these
complex math problems

00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:31.250
that secures the Bitcoin network.

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:33.300
What these mining farms do
is they're able to do things

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.340
in bulk.

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:35.690
If we do it at scale,

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:38.910
the odds are that we'll
eventually win the lottery.

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:39.940
- [Narrator] So crypto mining farms

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:42.860
are usually made up of thousands
of specialized computers

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:44.850
and the miners who get
the right answers first

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:47.080
are rewarded with new cryptocurrencies.

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:49.930
And these new coins can be
then sold on to exchanges.

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:52.280
The vast majority of
these specialized machines

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:54.100
have been manufactured in China,

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:56.300
giving miners there a
quicker and cheaper access

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:57.760
than others around the world.

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.900
- These computers are
consuming a lot of electricity.

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:01.880
It was so appealing to mine in China

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:03.680
because of the almost free power

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:05.780
from these hydro plants, for example.

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:08.640
- [Narrator] So with easy access
to both machines and power,

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:10.540
a large share of global Bitcoin mining

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:12.100
has happened in China.

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:14.040
The Beijing's tightening
grip on the industry

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:17.410
is forcing its homegrown
miners to look for a way out.

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:20.410
Since 2017, crypto trading
has been outlawed in China

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:21.770
because of the potential risks

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:24.090
cryptocurrencies pose
to financial stability

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:26.240
and the possibility of
the assets being used

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:28.120
for illegal activities.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:30.600
And now mining has come into sharper focus

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:32.810
because of the massive amount
of electricity consumed

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:35.460
by farms, posing a threat
to Beijing's commitment

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:37.200
to limit its carbon footprint.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.960
So miners in China are selling
their machines overseas

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:42.560
or moving their operations
to countries like the U.S,

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:44.360
Russia and Kazakhstan.

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:47.560
This exit from China has
benefited miners elsewhere.

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:50.710
- We are immediately earning
more Bitcoins every day.

00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:52.680
- [Narrator] Ben Gagnon
is a Chief Mining Officer

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:53.690
at Bitfarms.

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:56.600
A publicly traded Bitcoin
mining company in Canada.

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:58.670
And he says business after
Beijing's announcement

00:02:58.670 --> 00:02:59.960
has been booming.

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:02.010
- It is still kind of hard to believe

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:05.120
that all of this equipment came offline

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:08.610
as that market share and the
hash rate has been cut in half.

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:12.030
Our share of the Bitcoin
revenues has effectively doubled.

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:12.863
- [Narrator] This has also meant

00:03:12.863 --> 00:03:14.190
access to some of the best machines

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:15.580
that were once hard to get.

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:17.640
- All the machines that
are being manufactured

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:20.310
and are contracted to
these Chinese customers

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:23.060
that no longer have a
place to be installed.

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:24.640
- [Narrator] Prices of
these mining machines

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.830
have also dropped substantially.

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:28.810
For instance, one of
the most popular models,

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:31.030
which used to cost more than $10,000

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:33.480
was available for around half the price.

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:35.330
With the market awash with cheap machines,

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:37.810
Gagnon says crypto miners
are looking to expand

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:40.020
across North America and Central Asia.

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:42.410
- All around the world, I
think people are excited.

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:44.140
They're looking to gain that market share,

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:46.450
and either you can work
with Chinese miners

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:49.320
or to purchase their equipment from them

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:51.530
and earn that revenue for themselves.

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:53.240
- [Narrator] But expansion
comes with one big item

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:54.970
that isn't so easy to come by.

00:03:54.970 --> 00:03:57.100
- [Ben] Now, the bottleneck
is really on power.

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:58.680
So if you buy these machines

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:00.550
and you don't have a
place to plug them in,

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:03.151
it's not really a good
use of your investment.

00:04:03.151 --> 00:04:04.870
- [Narrator] Gagnon says,
it's a race against time

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:06.630
to set up the power infrastructure

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:08.880
before other miners come back online.

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:10.960
- 'Cause it just takes a lot longer

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:13.400
to develop this infrastructure
outside of China.

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:15.490
A lot of groups are doing
what we're doing right now,

00:04:15.490 --> 00:04:17.480
and they're focusing on
the energy infrastructure.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:20.110
They need to negotiate it,
they need to secure the permit.

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:22.760
So it's a long path forward.

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:24.440
- [Narrator] But the
crypto industry overseas

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:26.720
could face similar pressures as in China.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:28.020
For instance, in the U.S,

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:30.660
authorities have proposed
plans to hold crypto exchanges

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:33.120
to the same standards as
traditional securities

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:34.490
and financial services.

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:36.760
Well, some local communities
have expressed concerns

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:39.780
about the environmental
impact of mining facilities.

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:41.460
Despite the challenges ahead,

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:43.380
once these new mining farms are created,

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:45.900
crypto mining will likely
no longer be concentrated

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:47.180
in just one place.

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:50.360
- Concentration in China is
the most dangerous outcome

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:51.780
because as you can see

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:54.690
the entire mining industry
in that state can shut down.

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:56.250
- [Narrator] As for
China's homegrown miners,

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:57.720
the once golden place for mining

00:04:57.720 --> 00:04:59.920
will become a less viable option.

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:02.240
- These miners in China are
now looking for new homes

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:04.350
in favor of places that are secure.

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:07.250
They know the costs are far
too high, they need stability.

